<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Really. But you don\'92t even know what role I have imagined for you yet.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I have. I have imagined it.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Make your pitch,\'94 Eloise said, almost taunting.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Your Gyges Disc project.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What of it?\'94 Eloise thought better than to try denying she had such a project.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I want in.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You want in.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I want to run it.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Eloise blurted a laugh. \'93Of course you do.\'94 Eloise called the waiter over. \'93Devonshire Tea for four, please. And a bottle of champagne, please. At room temperature.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Yes, ma\'92am.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93So you agree to my terms?\'94 Sarah pushed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Sarah, my dear. I\'92d already considered allowing all that, and much more besides.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93And what of Hayley\'92s position?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Eloise addressed Hayley. \'93Assuming I can keep you from offshore detention for the crime you committed last night\'85 as Sarah\'92s Chief Security Officer, what would your first task be?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley thought quickly. \'93I presume you have the resources to locate people?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Eloise became stoic at the na\'efvet\'e9 of the question.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Anyone?\'94 Hayley pressed. \'93Anyone on the planet?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Eloise allowed herself a tight smile and a small shrug, which Hayley took to mean, indefatigably yes.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Good.\'94 Hayley\'92s analytical mind raced. \'93Then my first and highest priority is to stick it up Fridge Force.\'94
